<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Roxolani</h1><p class="st-meta">150 BCE – 375 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Sarmatian people of the steppe between the Don and the Danube, famous for heavy cavalry and repeated raids on Roman Moesia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Roxolani were one of the main Sarmatian tribes, first recorded between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-river">Don</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> in the 2nd century BCE. Under their leader Tasius they fought on the Scythian side against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diophantes">Diophantes</a>, general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI</a>, around 107 BCE. Over the following century they moved west towards the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sarmatians">Sarmatians</a> they were mounted pastoralists ruled by kings and nobles. Roman writers describe their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">lancers</a> in scale armour, terrifying in a charge but helpless when unhorsed. Their relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> swung between raids across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and treaties paid for with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 69 CE a large Roxolani raid into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> was destroyed in winter, and Hadrian later restored payments to their king Rasparaganus. Gothic expansion in the 3rd century and the Hunnic invasion of the 370s broke them up, and their remnants merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/roxolani.jpg" alt="Roxolani" width="320" height="266"><figcaption>Image: Andrein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Empire_125.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>150 BCE – 375 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tasius, Rasparaganus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sarmatian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sarmatian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/moldova">Moldova</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rhoxolani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=112&amp;focus=roxolani" aria-label="Roxolani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5285 573 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Roxolani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5605 829h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5605 829h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=112&amp;focus=roxolani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

